-- title:
--   Integrality over the node ring over A ∩ K
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, $A$ a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, $k$ a field of characteristic $q$ and $\mathrm{red} \colon A \to k$ a ring homomorphism; let $a \in k$ and let $K$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ of finite degree over $\mathbb Q$. Let $f$ lie in `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * q)`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the full modular function field of level $1 \cdot q$ inside the Laurent series field over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$. Assume: the Laurent series $f$ lies in `fieldOver (1 * q) K`, the subfield generated by the constant series from $K$ together with the two series $j$ and $j_q$; both $f$ and its image under `frickeInvolutionBar (1 * q)` (the base change of the chosen Fricke automorphism of level $1 \cdot q$) lie in `CharPReduction.modularLocalized (1 * q) A.toSubring red`, the localisation of the modular ring over $A$ at the prime ideal of elements killed by coefficientwise reduction, i.e. each is a quotient $r/s$ with $r, s$ in that modular ring and $s$ not in the reduction kernel; and for every place $W$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * q)` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ (a proper valuation subring containing the base field and a principal ideal ring) with $\operatorname{ord}_W f < 0$, it is not the case that simultaneously some $x \in A$ with $\mathrm{red}\,x = a$ has $\operatorname{ord}_W(j - x) > 0$ and some $y \in A$ with $\mathrm{red}\,y = a^{q}$ has $\operatorname{ord}_W(j_q - y) > 0$, where $j$ is the image under `coeffEmb` of the $q$-expansion `jq` and $j_q$ the image of `qExpand ℚ (1 * q) jq`. The conclusion is that $f$ is integral over the subring `modularLocalizedAtPoint (1 * q) (coeffSubring A K) (redRestrict red K) a (a ^ q)`, consisting of those Laurent series $g$ for which $g \cdot \mathrm{modularEval}(s) = \mathrm{modularEval}(r)$ for some two-variable polynomials $r, s$ over $A \cap K$ with $\mathrm{pointEval}$ of $s$ at $(a, a^{q})$, via the restriction of $\mathrm{red}$ to $A \cap K$, nonzero.
--
--   This is the normality (algebraic Hartogs) statement for the plane model $j, j_q$ of $X_0(q)$ in its form over a number field: a function defined over $K$, with no pole along the special fibre and no pole centred at the point $(a, a^{q})$ of the special fibre, is integral over the local ring of the model at that point, taken over $A \cap K$ rather than over $A$. It feeds the membership criteria [`ModularCurve.NodeLocalized.mem_modularLocalizedAtPoint_coeffSubring_of_isIntegral_of_mem_fieldOver`](thm.html#ModularCurve.NodeLocalized.mem_modularLocalizedAtPoint_coeffSubring_of_isIntegral_of_mem_fieldOver) and its variants, which place such functions in the descended node ring in which the local analysis at a supersingular point is carried out.
